# GitHub-only native static releases

The canonical release identity is defined in `release/versions.json`.

Official release tag:

    application-image-compilation/v1.0.0

Official release repository:

    https://github.com/Portfoligno/hell-application-image-compilation/releases

The protected tag workflow builds exactly two native static archives:

    hell-application-image-compilation-1.0.0-hell-2026-05-29-x86_64-linux-static.tar.xz
    hell-application-image-compilation-1.0.0-hell-2026-05-29-aarch64-linux-static.tar.xz

The x86_64 archive is built and executed on `ubuntu-24.04`. The aarch64
archive is built and executed on GitHub's native `ubuntu-24.04-arm` runner.
Cross-built output is never published as a release asset.

For a local native release-candidate build:

    nix build --no-update-lock-file .#release-static-native --out-link result-release

That command does not publish and does not make the result an official
artifact. Official publication requires an annotated protected tag on green
`main`, a tag workflow that creates or verifies a draft containing exactly six
assets, maintainer review, the Releases page **Publish release** button, and
successful read-only post-publication verification.

Consumer verification:

    sha256sum --check SHA256SUMS
    gh attestation verify <archive> -R Portfoligno/hell-application-image-compilation
    gh release verify application-image-compilation/v1.0.0 \
      -R Portfoligno/hell-application-image-compilation

Repository owners must enable immutable releases, protect `main`, restrict
creation/update/deletion of `application-image-compilation/v*` tags, require
the `metadata`, `test (x86_64-linux)`, and `test (aarch64-linux)` checks, and
configure Pages for GitHub Actions. No Actions `release` environment is used:
only a maintainer may publish a reviewed draft from the Releases page.
